From a155a93bb2077686ded0d6e5e317ffc3c8d80f7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mita5358 <kafitcohr@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:48:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/20] feat(dsh): expand a collapsed chunk on sight while
 scrolling
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A collapsed chunk used to seed one prompt placeholder row per turn, so a
restored transcript read as user-only history: 116 placeholder rows stood
in front of 119 real prompts, and every older turn looked like it had no
answer at all.

Seed one row per unloaded chunk instead - its digest line, marked
`collapsed` - and let that row expand on sight: MessageList picks the
collapsed row nearest the viewport middle, waits 120 ms of quiet, and asks
the channel to materialise that chunk in place (one chunk per scroll
gesture, never while following the tail). The row becomes a `▾` heading
followed by the real turns, so scrolling back reads like the conversation.

Gate: verify:history-chunks now pins the seed shape (one collapsed row per
chunk, id == idBase, no fake user rows, ids inside the chunk stride) and
that a materialised chunk carries real assistant rows.
